UNIX -> UROS
------------
ls -> dir
cat -> cat
echo -> puts
cd -> cd
mv -> move
mv -r -> md(MoveDirectory)
cp -> copy
cp -r -> cpd(CopyDirectory)
touch -> mkfile
mkdir -> makedir
find -> listtree
tree -> tree
rsync -> copytree(TempleOS Fork)
mount -> mnt (Since we have different Volumes in Eden(our filesystem remember?), 'Eden' is the main/master
volume while the mount volume would be 'mount' ie. [Mount:/]# instead of [Eden:/]# , cool right?)
file -> typeof
grep -> fsi (Find in Standard-In)
exec -> run (This would be used to execute UROS Scripts(basically URSL but yet 'run' will call the 'urlsc' compiler, JIT Compile whatever file was
passed as parameter, and run it immediately and when it's done is deletes the .ubin/.bin executable but still leaves the .urslc/.urc source code or "script" in that use case))

[Note: The default editor is going to be open through the 'buffer' command]
